      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense in theory, but when you're looking at actual market modeling, isn't there still a practical tendency to see multi-ethnic nations in these developing regions as \"higher risk\" compared to, say, a more unified Western or Asian nation? I mean, even if it's not \"inherent,\" isn't the historical reality that these multi-ethnic profiles in the Global South are much more prone to tribalism and sudden shifts in power that can disrupt investments? How do you account for that \"chaos factor\" in a professional risk report?",
